[orchestrator -> mcp__qa__request_approval] {"plan_summary":"Collection: \"Restful-Booker Checkin/Checkout Date Filter Tests (agent-built)\"\n\nTC01 (setup) POST /auth: log in as admin and save the token.…

================ PLAN FOR REVIEW ================
Collection: "Restful-Booker Checkin/Checkout Date Filter Tests (agent-built)"

TC01 (setup) POST /auth: log in as admin and save the token. Expect 200 and a non-empty token.
TC02 (setup) POST /booking: create a booking with a unique name, check-in 2027-06-10 and check-out 2027-06-15. Expect 200 and save bookingId.
TC03 (positive) GET /booking?checkin=2027-06-09 (one day before check-in): the booking should be in the results.
TC04 (edge) GET /booking?checkin=2027-06-10 (same day as check-in, docs say ">="): the booking should be in the results.
TC05 (negative) GET /booking?checkin=2027-06-11 (one day after check-in): the booking should NOT be in the results.
TC06 (positive) GET /booking?checkout=2027-06-14 (one day before check-out): the booking should be in the results.
TC07 (edge) GET /booking?checkout=2027-06-15 (same day as check-out, docs say ">="): the booking should be in the results.
TC08 (negative) GET /booking?checkout=2027-06-16 (one day after check-out): the booking should NOT be in the results.
TC09 (positive) GET /booking?checkin=2027-06-10&checkout=2027-06-15 (both exact dates): the booking should be in the results.
TC10 (negative) GET /booking?checkin=2027-06-01&checkout=2027-06-16 (check-in matches, check-out does not): the booking should NOT be in the results.
TC11 (edge) GET /booking?checkin=2999-01-01 (far future): expect 200 and an empty list [].
TC12 (edge) GET /booking?checkout=2999-01-01 (far future): expect 200 and an empty list [].
TC13 (cleanup) DELETE /booking/{{bookingId}} using the token cookie: expect 201.
TC14 (cleanup) GET /booking/{{bookingId}}: expect 404, which confirms the booking was deleted.

Notes: these cases follow the docs, which say both filters match dates ">=" the given date. If the live API behaves differently, the run will flag that as a gap between the docs and the API. For filters that don't pin down one booking, the cases only check whether our booking is present or absent, because the server is shared.
